- **Brom's "Held," (43:87)** is new speech of mine, written to make "Two words… Both of them ours" true to what has just been said in the cut. If the two words are meant to be others, that one line and the sentence after it are the whole of the dependency.
- **"Lie still when I say. That's still the term." moved** to the send-off (permitted by the brief).
