editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:576:## AFTER MOVEMENT 6 — chapters 34–40, days 291–293 (drafted 2026-10-11, author claude-opus-5-5, NO-SOURCE method)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:578:### Coordinator rulings (binding)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:579:- **Entry seam with Movement 5 ratified** (Sol plan audit): the loft on the night of the 290th; eleven fragments; deployment thirty-two; purse 134; Vastin's knee re-splinted; Karis's left palm stitched; the fifty-two sheets on their three tables.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:581:- **How the twelfth behaves (ruled against the audit).** **It leans at every made thing, unbidden, outward** — the board, a rope-walk, a bridge, a hinge, a table — and Cael is learning not to look ("it looks before I've said that it may"). That is the plan's own wording ("the twelfth leans at every made thing … He learns not to look"; "catches himself reading made things everywhere") and stands. **It has never been turned inward, on Cael's own still place**, and he refused that turn once, deliberately, until Oryn has been asked. **The first INWARD turn is unbidden and belongs to Millrace (Movement 7).** It has never been used on a person, the crown or the leaf. A few unmeant outward glances (the rope-walk on the night of the 291st; Hesk's dividers; the inn table) are not counted as deployments.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:597:### Review record
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:600:### New canon minted (author's list)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:627:- **Cleon's day over.** At the bell of the 293rd: "They lie tonight… I said a week. I'll be a day over it. There's the back of that skin to do." (To meet the next packet's 294th.)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:633:### State at movement end (author; governed by the rulings above and by the surviving prose)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:666:### Next-movement inheritance (Sol plan audit §8; also written into the next packet)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:667:Movement 7 already carries the 294th, all-day list, twelve fragments, Karis's bound hand, Vastin day fifteen and no mule (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:28–30`). Its author must additionally inherit:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:670:- **Fragments and knowledge.** Twelve fragments; deployment thirty-two. The eleventh remains unused and known to Lira through the log but not Vastin. The twelfth is known to Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Cleon; Oryn and Vastin have not been told. Cleon knows how this one fragment came but no other acquisition history. The warning is known only to Cael and Cleon and is in no book (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:197–239,279–339`; `manuscript/chapter-36.md:15–63`; `manuscript/chapter-37.md:219–227`). **Coordinator ruling (overrides the audit here):** the twelfth leans at made things UNBIDDEN and OUTWARD in Movement 6 (the board, the rope-walk, the bridge, the dividers, the inn table), and Cael is learning not to look; a few unmeant outward glances are on the page and are not counted as deployments. It has never been turned INWARD, and he refused that turn once, deliberately, until Oryn has been asked. Movement 7's beat is the first INWARD turn, and it comes unbidden.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:671:- **Cleon.** He has shown the Path's inside, been told the twelfth's mechanism, declined a dangerous sentence, given the warning, deliberately looked away for two days, promised the leaf stays under his hand and above no counter, and said “Tomorrow the rest of the leaf. The list of parts.” (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:15–239`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:115–125,227–239`). He let the fifty-two sheets lie one extra night and has written the 294th card (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:117–125`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:683:## AFTER MOVEMENT 7 — chapters 41–46, days 294–299 (drafted 2026-10-12, author claude-opus-5-5, NO-SOURCE method)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:685:### Coordinator rulings (binding)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:686:- **Entry seam with Movement 6 ratified** (Sol plan audit): twelve fragments; deployment thirty-two; purse 130; the loft and handcart to the 295th; the leaf's back unread; Vastin's knee day fourteen on the 293rd; Karis's stitched palm; Brom's arms; Lira's days out of wool; sixty yards of rope owed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:687:- **The 294th: the list of parts.** Cleon turned the skin between boards; its back is paler, scored and not inked, **nine short lines, a thing and its number to each**. Karis can spell all nine and turn four (the four things the face says were made); the other five are spelled and unturned, and **she has said none of the numbers aloud**. **The fourth line is the mark's:** the word for the mark is what bears; two runs hang from it LEVEL (those who are kindled; and a six-sign word in the scraped-thin place), and after both the number *three*. Cleon made a second copy, drawn and not read, and gave it to Karis ("Your hand's better than mine on the fourth line."). The fifty-two sheets were counted into three boxes under two hands, K. and V. The clerk wrote *Withdrawn by its bearer* and *four* and ruled the account off. Protected, Cleon's, at the iron door: "Work. Not a finding." / "Mind the stair. It leans." **He is not above ground and did not look at Cael.** This edition has no noun "bearer" for a sign (signs bear, are carried, or are nothing).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:689:- **How Vastin travelled (ruled against the audit).** After the alley his knee would not carry him a day's road: **he rode the rope-walk dray's tail-board for three days at a copper a day of his own, got down for every hill, and walked the whole cut**; on the 298th Teague put him on a salt cart ("It's owed a seat. For him. I'll not walk ten at the pace of one."). **From the ford on the 299th he walks in the file.** The packet's "walked again on a bad knee" is met by the hills and the cut; closed Movement 6 (a rope down a ladder, a stall, a handcart, a stair on his seat) governs the rest.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:701:- **Dawn, the 299th.** "Twelve," … "And a mule." (Seln). The mule carries the three boxes, the flat, a sack of meal, Oryn's pannier and canvas. Karis pinned a clean sheet to the hide's eastern edge, pricked the divider's point on it, and ruled the pencil line from the fourth ring through the point and a hand's breadth past ("I am not going to draw a stop that the paper does not give me").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:702:- **Bodies at dawn on the 299th.** Vastin: **day twenty of thirty**, Oryn's linen and two laths, stick, walking. Brom: both arms up to the shoulder. Lira: the arm released. Karis: stitches out, linen on, not to lean. Teague: the right wrist in linen under the leather. Cael: sound.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:705:### Review record
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:708:### New canon minted (author's list)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:711:- **The back of the leaf (41:29–49; 41:55–59; 41:113–135).** Paler than the face, with no dark stuff rubbed in; nine short lines in a column down the left side, ruled first; each a noun and a number written out in words. The first four begin with the four things that the face names, in the face's order; the other five are nouns that Karis can spell and cannot turn. No number is said aloud. The fourth line (the mark's) crosses the thin place behind the scraping: one bearer (the face's word for the mark), two runs hung level from it (five signs; six signs), and the number *three*. On the 294th the first run is "the people at a kindling"; of the second, three signs of six are sure. Nobody asks whether the back sits or goes; Cleon says only that it is a list, that the two runs hang level, and that it ends ("There's no tenth that's been cut away").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:747:### State at movement end (author; governed by the rulings above and by the surviving prose)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:756:**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. No grey. **Left shoulder mended by Oryn** on the 298th; **right re-tied by the older healer** in two yards; both arms come up to his shoulders on the 299th. He paid the rope debt and gave Pike the thumbed slip. **The purse: a hundred and twenty-seven.** Oryn's bowl is back with her.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:762:**Vastin.** No office; no age stated. **Right knee: day twenty of thirty on the 299th**; Oryn's linen and two new laths; the slat is off; the month stands as counted. He stood on the leg once, with the stick up, at the line in the cut (the 296th). He rode the dray's tail-board for three days at a copper a day, and the salt cart on the 298th at Teague's ruling; he walks every hill. He kept the tally of the fifty-two sheets and signed it V. He sat before the six at the halting-ground and laid no copper. He took Oryn's "Stand there." without a clause and stood an hour. He has said "Noted." once (45:165; marker 15 may hold a second). He told Oryn of the wall of the eleventh day himself. He is on Teague's count of ten as one of "your six"; that is a count for a contract; he has not asked to join the six and nobody has spoken of it. He has been offered a seat at the shoulder hold's fire and has not answered. **He does not know** the mechanism, the eleventh, the twelfth, the two words, the date, or what is under the bar; he knows that he is not told, and that it is "six people's". He stopped the sentence about the mark twice more, without a word.
