--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-36.md-38-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-36.md-39-"Yes. It's not mine to put there."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-36.md-40-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-36.md-41-She gave the book back, and she did not look pleased, and she did not ask again; he thought that it had cost her something not to, and was sorry, and could not mend it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-36.md-42-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-36.md:43:Seln had heard the whole of that from the ladder's head, where he sat with his feet on the second rung, as he sat every evening.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-36.md-44-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-36.md-45-"You have a twelfth," he said. "And you have told a registered practitioner of the Compact, beneath its oldest registry, how you came by it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-36.md-46-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-36.md-47-"How I came by that one. Nothing of the rest, and nothing of any of you. I asked the three who were there. I couldn't ask you."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-36.md-48-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-36.md-49-"What did he do with it?"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-36.md-50-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-36.md-51-"He gave me a cup of water, and went back to his board."
