editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-35.md-254-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-35.md:255:For eight days those red eyes had gone over him as water goes over a stone in a ford. He had been a hook, and a hook is not looked at; he had asked to be exactly that, and had minded it, and had written that he minded. They had not gone over him tonight. When the cup was set down they had come to the edge of him. They had come as far as a sleeve, and the wrist of the hand that held the light; and there they had stopped, and the man had turned his whole head away to the oak, as a person turns from a lit window that is not his to look in at.
