editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-35.md-335-He had not lied to the man by the width of a hair. He stood on a tread that he could not see, with a box dragging at his shoulders and a strap in his fist, and waited to be asked how he came to know the length of it.
