editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-26.md:59:"It's a very good view. I'd have given everything I had for it. I very nearly did." Her left hand had come out of its pocket, and she looked at that for a moment, the long thin fingers that had been in wool for the better part of half a year, and shut them. "I've carried fifty-two sheets up the inside of it, and seen who fetches its eggs. You can't want a place the same once you've been its porter. I don't think you can, anyway."
