editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-22.md:259:She did not sleep at once. There had been a Gold, in a bed by a window, with a wrenched wrist. It had not even been broken. He had had six healers' attention on the first morning, and had gone home before noon; and a woman from the river sheds had waited three nights at the bottom of a heap. Oryn had walked out of a gate to be quit of those sums.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-22.md-260-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-22.md-261-A carter had waited a whole cold term, with a crooked wrist, for want of her.
