editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-19.md:37:"Provisional. I never stayed to have it confirmed." She rubbed her palms together slowly. "It was a house for the sick, inside a wall, with forty beds and six of us to tend them. Every bed in it had a sheet on a board at its foot. There was the name on it, and the complaint, and what had been spent. And there was a column for the patient's tier."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-19.md-38-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-19.md-39-"For the patient's," said Karis. Her pencil was not in her hand.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-19.md-40-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-19.md-41-"Not for the healer's. For theirs. I filled that column in for a long while before I asked what it was for; I thought that it was like the name. Then there was a week of fever in the low town, and the house was full to the stairs, and I found out." She spoke as she spoke a finding. "We'd so much in us, the six of us together, as I've so much in me tonight, and it had to be spent on somebody. It went down the column from the top. There was a Gold in a bed by the window with a wrenched wrist. He had what he wanted on the first day. Then the Silvers had theirs."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-19.md-42-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-19.md-43-Nobody at the fire moved.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-19.md-44-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-19.md:45:"There was a woman brought in from the river sheds on the third night. She'd no tier that anybody could find. She'd never been stood on a plate, or her paper was lost; I never knew which. So there was nothing to put in the column." Oryn's eyes had gone to the peats. "A sheet with an empty column goes to the bottom of the heap. It's not cruelty. It's only how a heap is sorted."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-19.md-46-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-19.md-47-"Did she die?" said Lira, very low.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-19.md-48-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-19.md-49-"She did not. I'll not have you think it worse than it was. I went to her at night, off the sheet, with what I had left, and it was enough. And in the morning the woman who kept that house showed me the board, where there was a spending and no tier written against it. She said that a healer who spends off the sheet has stolen from whoever stood next on it." Her spoon was in her hand, and she turned it over. "She was right. That's the thing that I've never got past. By that house's sums she was right, and I couldn't fault a line of them. So I went to look for some other sums."
