editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-19.md-87-She came round the fire then. She stopped at her stride and a half from Cael, and he saw her mouth open; and he knew the sentence before it came, not by its words but by its shape, since he had watched it arrive in her three times and be shut in.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-19.md-88-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-19.md-89-This time she did not shut it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-19.md-90-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-19.md:91:"You said a station, at that board. He said it first, by the fire, and then with a bowl turned over. I know stations. There's one on the crown of every city inside the Line, with steps going up to it and a square in front, and I've stood in such a square with a line of children and watched them go up one at a time." She did not push up her sleeves. "It's the one thing in a town that's built to read whatever is brought near it. And I've had my hands on you, a long while back, and I found a thing that I made you write down and leave alone. I've not touched it since. I don't know what it is."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-19.md-92-
