    17	She looked at the bank. She counted. He watched her do it, because he had watched her count a crew on a bank before and knew the order she took them in: Lira, whose arm she had priced at a fork; Brom, whose shoulder she had not been allowed to bind; Karis, whose hand was bound and had not been when she left; Seln; and then the man with the stick, and the stick, and the knee under the trouser, and the look went to the knee and stayed there a moment longer than it had on anything else, and then came to Cael, and stopped.
    18	
    19	"Six," she said, and he said it back.
    20	
    21	"And five that aren't." The look went past him, to the road, where Teague's four stood with the tall woman's spear grounded and the young one looking at the ford as the young look at everything, and to the fifth, the older woman with the cloth bag, who was looking at the lean-to as a woman looks at another woman's table. Oryn looked at her. The older woman looked back. It lasted as long as it took, and neither of them nodded, and neither of them looked away first, and then the older woman looked at Brom's shoulder, once, as she had looked at it in a marsh and across a room, and Oryn looked at it too, and then they had both looked at the same thing and priced it the same, and that was the whole of the exchange between the two healers on the bearing, then or after, and Cael entered it as complete.
    22	
    23	"The rest," Oryn said, to the bank, to the six of them, in the register, "can wait till I've done the line. Sit down. Not you." That was to Vastin. "You stand there and don't put the stick down, because you've been putting it down, I can see it from here, and I said a month."
    24	
    25	"Nineteen days," Vastin said.
    26	
    27	"Then it's eleven more. Stand there."
    28	
    29	He stood there. It was, Cael thought, the first order the man had taken since a cut without walking it back, and he took it from a woman at a plank table with her hands in a pan, and stood, and did not say anything about it, and Cael noted the date.
    30	
