    86	
    87	"Held," he said, low.
    88	
    89	The old man looked from the big man to the stones. He had said one word in that cut, and had been given one. Seventeen days ago, on the same ground, the loudest thing on the whole moor had been his.
    90	
    91	"Two words," Vastin said. "Both of them ours."
    92	
    93	"Noted," Cael said.
