   154	
   155	"You're on my side."
   156	
   157	Cael looked at where his own boots were. The room had pressed in behind Brom, and he had been carried round the bench's end with the press, and had fetched up at the one-armed man's elbow, on the side where the candle was. He had read two leaves of that ledger over the stump of an arm. Every line of them had lain the right way up, and he had not once marked it.
   158	
   159	"I'll go round."
   160	
   161	"Stop where you are. It reads the same from there. I never said that it didn't."
   162	
