+The repaired movement is clear to the fluent-thirteen-year-old lens and the adult progression reader except for the two line defects. The protected dialogue now arrives as story rather than production markup. Speakers are audible, especially at the cut, the contract, the grade, the Millrace treatments, and the leaf refusal. The narrow referent pass improves chapters 41 and 46 without making the narration over-explain.
+
+The annual-sheet phrase is a real one-pass logic failure: a reader hears **“one sheet to a year”** and then, twenty-six lines later, hears that the form proves no annual visit. Removing it leaves the intended, comprehensible distinction between a series-year and an annual field sheet. The ladder reference creates a false picture of a closed action; “stair” restores the remembered event and makes Oryn's “second time” exchange land cleanly.
+
+Oryn's house memory reads as character history rather than exposition, and “thirty rounds” does not yield a hidden age. Her route timing is intelligible. The contract count, healer exclusions, march order, and dawn count reconcile on one pass. I would continue reading; the eastward line, watcher pressure, incompatible findings, and withheld next word remain strong forward pulls.
